body:
Arrow-key navigation uses `schema.widgets[index ± 1]`, but `index` comes from the render loop and is relative to the list being mapped. In the mobile layout, widgets are mapped from filtered subsets (metrics vs others), so `index` won’t match the position in `schema.widgets` and navigation can jump to the wrong widget. Consider deriving the current index from `widgetId` (e.g., `findIndex`) before computing next/prev.
```suggestion
      // Derive the position from widgetId to avoid relying on subset indices
      const currentIndex =
        widgetId != null ? widgets.findIndex((w) => w.id === widgetId) : -1;

      if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') {
        e.preventDefault();
        onWidgetClick(widgetId ?? null);
      } else if (e.key === 'ArrowRight' || e.key === 'ArrowDown') {
        e.preventDefault();
        if (currentIndex === -1) return;
        const nextIndex = currentIndex + 1;
        const next = nextIndex < widgets.length ? widgets[nextIndex] : null;
        if (next?.id) onWidgetClick(next.id);
      } else if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft' || e.key === 'ArrowUp') {
        e.preventDefault();
        if (currentIndex === -1) return;
        const prevIndex = currentIndex - 1;
        const prev = prevIndex >= 0 ? widgets[prevIndex] : null;
```
